"""Exact museum exhibits and Mansion diary entries, read in their own order."""
ROWS=[]
def add(key,label,subject,lines):
    replies=[s.strip() for s in lines.split('|')]
    assert len(replies)==11,(key,len(replies))
    ROWS.append(dict(key='kanto_lore_object_'+key,labels=[label],subject=subject,replies=replies))
add('jungle_discovery','PokemonMansion_1F_Text_NewMonDiscoveredInGuyanaJungle','A July fifth diary records discovering a new Pokemon deep in a Guyana jungle.',
"They must have been so excited when they wrote this. I wonder what happened after that.|The entry gives a date and a location, but little about the observation itself.|An exciting discovery. It still deserved careful handling.|You can almost hear someone trying to fit an enormous day onto a small page.|I hope their first thought included whether the Pokemon was all right.|A confident beginning, found in a house that makes us uneasy about the rest.|The beginning sounds so much brighter than the room it was left in.|A field discovery needs records detailed enough for someone else to check.|A living thing existed before someone arrived to call it a discovery.|They found something new to them. That does not mean it became theirs.|I wish the entry described the jungle around the Pokemon, too.")
add('mew_name','PokemonMansion_1F_Text_ChristenedDiscoveredMonMew','A July tenth diary records naming the newly discovered Pokemon Mew.',
"Mew. A tiny name for a day somebody clearly wanted to remember.|Assigning a name helps a record, but is only the beginning of understanding the subject.|Naming it was the easy part. Treating it well mattered more.|It is a soft little name. I hope someone said it gently.|A name can make caring feel personal. I hope that happened here.|The unknown has acquired a name. It has not surrendered all its mysteries.|A short name, preserved long after the hand that wrote it left.|A useful label. Still not a substitute for learning what it needs.|A name placed beside a mystery, without making the mystery smaller.|I would like to know why they chose that name, rather than why they thought they could.|This feels like the sort of entry that once made its writer smile.")
add('mewtwo_birth','PokemonMansion_1F_Text_MewGaveBirthToMewtwo','A February sixth diary records Mew giving birth and naming the newborn Mewtwo.',
"A newborn should have had someone looking out for it, however extraordinary it was.|The record describes a birth and a name. It does not describe how the newborn was cared for.|A new life needed care. Power would not change that.|The name makes it sound like a second version. I hope somebody saw an individual.|New life means responsibility, not just an exciting result.|A newborn enters the record already defined in relation to someone else.|A name with a number in it can carry a very heavy expectation.|The missing care details concern me more than the naming convention.|A new life arrived. That should have changed what the people here owed it.|I hope it was allowed to be more than the reason everyone was excited.|I wish this entry told us who stayed with it on its first night.")
add('mewtwo_power','PokemonMansion_B1F_Text_MewtwoIsFarTooPowerful','A September first diary calls Mewtwo too powerful and says attempts to curb its vicious tendencies failed.',
"This is frightening. It also sounds like nobody here knew how to help it.|The writer reports failed control and labels the behavior vicious. That is one perspective, not a full account of its causes.|They could not control it. That does not tell us everything about why it fought them.|There is fear in this entry. I wonder how much fear the Pokemon felt.|Whatever happened, a living creature needed more than people becoming afraid of their own responsibility.|The record has turned from discovery to control. That change deserves our attention.|The page names the creature dangerous. It leaves its own authors curiously unexamined.|A failed attempt at control needs investigation, including conditions and treatment.|A frightened page can preserve fear without preserving the whole truth.|I believe the danger was real. I do not think this single entry explains all of it.|I want to know what happened between the hopeful entries and this one.")
add('aerodactyl','PewterCity_Museum_1F_Text_AerodactylFossil','The exhibit identifies a rare ancient Aerodactyl fossil.',
"That once belonged to something that could move through the sky. Hard to picture it being still.|The specimen gives us evidence of an ancient Pokemon. Reconstruction still requires care.|Old bones. Once a living creature. Worth remembering both.|I keep trying to imagine the sound of those wings.|Something that lived so long ago still makes people stop and look.|An entrance preserved for ages after its performer left.|A long silence, shaped like something that once crossed the sky.|Physical remains can answer some questions and make entirely new ones.|Stone keeping the outline of a life the sky no longer remembers.|I like that a room full of strangers can still be impressed by it.|I wonder what a flying Pokemon today would notice about that shape.")
add('kabutops','PewterCity_Museum_1F_Text_KabutopsFossil','The exhibit identifies a rare ancient Kabutops fossil.',
"I am glad we can admire those sharp bits from this side of history.|An ancient body plan preserved well enough to study. Its unfamiliarity is part of the interest.|Impressive shape. Let the museum staff handle it.|It is strange how something so still can look ready to move.|I wonder what an ordinary day looked like for it, before it became an exhibit.|The past has arrived with a silhouette that needs no embellishment.|A very old creature still making the present feel a little less comfortable.|I would like to see how the preserved parts support their reconstruction.|An old life, with edges the years have not made gentle.|The label is calm about a shape that is doing quite a lot.|The details are easier to notice when I stop expecting it to resemble Pokemon I know.")
add('meteorite','PewterCity_Museum_1F_Text_MeteoriteThatFellOnMtMoon','The display describes a meteorite from Mt Moon thought to be a Moon Stone.',
"A rock that fell from the sky and still has people wondering about it. Good career.|Thought to be is the useful phrase. The identification is presented as tentative.|Look carefully. We do not need to touch it to be curious.|Something from very far away, ending up close enough for a child to point at.|I like a place that makes room for a question instead of rushing to sound certain.|A celestial arrival, followed by the much slower business of figuring out what arrived.|A long fall, ending in a small label with an honest uncertainty.|I would like to know which properties support the Moon Stone identification.|The sky left something behind, and the mountain gave it a place to land.|The label is allowed to admit it is not completely sure. Refreshing.|I wonder how different it looked when someone first found it on the mountain.")
add('shuttle','PewterCity_Museum_1F_Text_SpaceShuttle','The museum display is labelled Space Shuttle.',
"Someone looked all the way up and decided walking would not be enough.|A striking reminder of the engineering required to leave a familiar environment.|That took a lot of people doing their jobs properly.|I wonder what the last familiar sound was before launch.|A journey that makes packing lunch look wonderfully straightforward.|The largest possible answer to wanting to get out of the house.|An enormous machine built around a very old habit of looking up.|Now that is a collection of systems that had to work together.|A vessel built for a place where no ordinary road can be made.|Imagine trusting that many people with every part of the trip.|I wish I could see the faces of the people who watched its first launch.")
